    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-13802",
      "knowledge_point_id": "41b7d83f-3b9b-556c-9e49-13df9c3b597e",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Functions Containing the Natural Logarithm",
      "problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2x}\\cdot 2=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)|+C"
            },
