    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-346435",
      "knowledge_point_id": "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05",
      "knowledge_point": "Evaluating Definite Integrals",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $4$ | $32$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{4}^{32}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{2}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{u}\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =(2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2}"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "2\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{2}",
          "choices_complete": false,
          "correct_origin": "ma_successful_grade"
        }
      ],
